            <chunk name="Object" index="4">
              <items count="2">
                <item name="GUID" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">59e0b89a-e487-49f8-bab8-b5bab16be14c</item>
                <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
              </items>
              <chunks count="1">
                <chunk name="Container">
                  <items count="8">
                    <item name="Description" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">A panel for custom notes and text values</item>
                    <item name="InstanceGuid" type_name="gh_guid" type_code="9">39b0172c-7df2-4fbf-80b1-f75d9b2e1909</item>
                    <item name="Name" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Panel</item>
                    <item name="NickName" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Description</item>
                    <item name="Optional" type_name="gh_bool" type_code="1">false</item>
                    <item name="ScrollRatio" type_name="gh_double" type_code="6">0</item>
                    <item name="SourceCount" type_name="gh_int32" type_code="3">0</item>
                    <item name="UserText" type_name="gh_string" type_code="10">Purpose: Does an urban block's open space pass the BRE amenity test: at least half of it in two hours of sun on 21 March?
Fidelity: Screening - geometric ray casting, direct beam only; trees are left out, as BRE does.
Method: Site Context fetches Barnsbury, London, 2 m cells cover its ground zones; Sun Hours counts 21 March; Sunlight Compliance judges BRE amenity.
Result: Sun hours per cell on parks, gardens and squares in Flex Legend; PASS or FAIL in the report panel. Cells inside buildings count as unlit.
Needs: Nothing to install; runs inside Rhino. Runtime: minutes.
Edit: Site Picker location, Radius, grid Spacing, Sunlight Compliance thresholds; Standard 1-3 switches to EN 17037.</item>
                  </items>
                  <chunks count="2">
                    <chunk name="Attributes">
                      <items count="5">
